{{also|Inquisition}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fro|inquisicion}}, from {{uder|en|la|inquisitio}}, from {{m|la|inquirere}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɪŋkwɪˈzɪʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-inquisition.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪʃən|s=4}}
* {{hyph|en|in|qui|si|tion}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[inquiry]] or [[investigation]] into the [[truth]] of some [[matter#Noun|matter]].
#* {{RQ:Latimer Lords Prayer|chapter=[The First Sermon]|folio=5|verso=1|folioend=6|folioref=5|versoref=1|passage=But as farrefoorth as I coulde learne, through earneſt '''inquiſition''' I thoughte in my conſcience the woman was not gilty, all the circumſtances well conſydered.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare As You Like It|act=II|scene=ii|passage=Let not search and '''inquisition''' quail / To bring again these foolish runaways.}}
# An [[inquest]].
# A [[questioning#Noun|questioning]].
# The [[finding#Noun|finding]] of a [[jury]], especially such a finding under a [[writ#Noun|writ]] of inquiry.
#* {{RQ:Blackstone Commentaries|passage=The justices in eyre had it formerly in charge to make '''inquisition''' concerning them by a jury of the county.}}

